x86_64-linux  An enumeration is still `int` here, which docs/CONFORMANCE.md records: the enumerators are constants of type int and there is no enumeration type behind them. So n::twice(Level) is spelled with its parameter as int where clang writes the enumeration - _ZN1n5twiceEi against _ZN1n5twiceENS_5LevelE, ?twice@n@@YAHH@Z against ?twice@n@@YAHW4Level@1@@Z. Every other name in the case agrees. This case is about where an enumeration may be written and how its names are found, which is what the fix was; giving one a type of its own is a separate step and it changes the mangling of every function that takes one.
